"Stefan Kalgraf" <mr_white2003@hotmail.com> writes:
> Hi, I've just started playing Nethack and the interface is a little
> overwhelming. I'm wondering a few things:
> 
> 1. is there some way to set what autopickup actually picks up? Basically I
> want to avoid picking up statues and chests, possibly weapons and armor as
> well.

As S. notes, the pickup_types option (you more likely want to set it
in your .nethackrc or moral equivalent rather than having to set it
with O each time, though). Note that it works at symbol granularity,
so you can tell it whether to pick up weapons or armour, but can't say
"all tools other than chests".

(I have it set to simply $, which I turn off in the late game; I can
always tweak it if there's something in particular I need to
autopickup in a given situation.)

> 2. Is there an option that will improve the inventory interface or is the
> default all there is(trying to make the transition from ADOM)?

That depends on your platform and what you consider an improvement :-)
You might want to look at 'fixinv', 'menustyle', 'sort_pack', and
'perm_invent' and make sure they're what you want them to be; also,
look at the 'menu_*' accelerator keys, which speed things up
immensely. All these options are documented in the Guidebook.

